Answer B Text: \( 9,712 \mathrm{~m} \)
Answer C Text: \( 4,020 \mathrm{~m} \)
Answer D Text: \( 17,476 \mathrm{~m} \)', 'correct_solution': 'First, find the combined height of Mount St. Martha and Glencoe Peak:\n\nSt. Martha: 8,368 m\nGlencoe Peak: 1,344 m\nCombined height = 8,368 + 1,344 = 9,712 m\n\nNow, find how much taller Kibo is than this combined height:\nKibo: 12,388 m\nDifference = 12,388 - 9,712 = 2,676 m\n\nSo, Kibo is 2,676 m taller than the combined height of St. Martha and Glencoe Peak.', 'incorrect_solution': '', 'self_correctness': 'Yes', 'self_typical_confusion': 3.0, 'self_typical_interactions': 3.0}

{'question': 'Question Text: What is the median number of siblings?
Question Image: \begin{tabular}{|c|c|} \hline Siblings(s) & Frequency \( (f) \) \\ \hline \( 0 \) & \( 4 \) \\ \hline \( 1 \) & \( 3 \) \\ \hline \( 2 \) & \( 9 \) \\ \hline \( 3 \) & \( 10 \) \\ \hline \( 4 \) & \( 7 \) \\ \hline \end{tabular}
Answer A Text: \( 4 \)
Answer B Text: \( 2 \)
Answer C Text: \( 3 \)
Answer D Text: \( 10 \)', 'correct_solution': "First, list out the data using the frequencies:\n\n- 0 siblings: 4 students\n- 1 sibling: 3 students\n- 2 siblings: 9 students\n- 3 siblings: 10 students\n- 4 siblings: 7 students\n\nTotal number of students = 4 + 3 + 9 + 10 + 7 = 33\n\nTo find the median, arrange all the data in order and find the middle value (the 17th value, since (33+1)/2 = 17).\n\nCumulative frequencies:\n- 0 siblings: 4\n- 1 sibling: 4 + 3 = 7\n- 2 siblings: 7 + 9 = 16\n- 3 siblings: 16 + 10 = 26\n- 4 siblings: 26 + 7 = 33\n\nThe 17th value falls in the '3 siblings' group (since up to 16 is '2 siblings', and 17th is the first in the '3 siblings' group).\n\nSo, the median number of siblings is 3.", 'incorrect_solution': '', 'self_correctness': 'Yes', 'self_typical_confusion': 3.0, 'self_typical_interactions': 3.0}

